# Distributed Background Job Processing Platform

A scalable background job processing platform that asynchronously accepts, queues, and executes long-running tasks using a distributed worker architecture. The system separates job submission from job execution using BullMQ and Redis, allowing multiple workers to process jobs concurrently while MongoDB maintains persistent job state, progress, execution history, and failure information.

A React-based monitoring dashboard provides real-time visibility into job execution using Socket.IO, allowing users to track job status and progress without manually refreshing the application.

## Overview

Traditional web applications can become slow or unresponsive when long-running operations are executed directly inside HTTP request handlers. This platform addresses that problem by moving resource-intensive tasks to background workers.

Instead of processing a task directly:

```text
Client
  |
  v
API
  |
  v
Long-Running Task
  |
  v
Response
```

the platform uses asynchronous job processing:

```text
Client
  |
  v
REST API
  |
  +----> MongoDB
  |
  v
BullMQ
  |
  v
Redis
  |
  v
Worker
  |
  v
Job Processing
  |
  v
MongoDB
```

This allows the API to remain responsive while workers independently process background tasks.

